@startuml mms_release_backport
title MMS / Cloud Monolith — Backport Release (overlay on existing dated branch)

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #EAF4E9
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4C8C4A
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F5F5F5

' Declare swimlanes up front to pin column order: Human (left) | Automated (right)
|Human|
|Automated|

|Human|
start

note right
  Backports are NOT a separate release train.
  No kickoff, no Slack poll, no branch cut.
  They ride the existing prod vYYYYMMDD branch
  and the same mms-prod-deploy.yml as the major train.
end note

:**Prepare backport**
cherry-pick / open PR onto the EXISTING prod
vYYYYMMDD branch (no new branch cut)
(version_manifest --backport, or emergency hot-fix);

:**Merge to dated branch**
staging pointer stays on same branch as prod
(staging branch == prod branch);

|Automated|
:**PROD GATE CHECK** — weekday cron walk-back
(mms-prod-deploy-trigger-cron.yml, cron '0 13 * * 1-5')
staging==prod branch -> NOT skip-release-week
newest green staging SHA ahead of prod;
note right
  This cron is the backport delivery mechanism.
  During a MAJOR release week staging/prod branches
  differ -> decision skip-release-week -> cron stands down.
  Cron currently commented out (TODO cutover);
  workflow_dispatch used today.
end note

if (eligible green SHA found?) then (yes)
  :dispatch mms-prod-deploy.yml (sha);
else (no-green-sha / already-current / in-flight)
  :HOLD — no deploy dispatched
  notify #cne-alerts;
  stop
endif

|Human|
:**PROD APPROVAL GATE**
mms-monolith-prod-deploy-approvers
(a human approves EVERY prod move);

|Automated|
partition "PROD" {
  fork
    :deploy group **dbs**;
  fork again
    :deploy group **resources**;
  end fork
  :deploy **web · backup(off) · billing** (WBB);
}
note right: via wt-deploy-mms-monolith-v2\n(identical to major train)

|Human|
:approve-continue;

|Automated|
partition "PROD-GOV" {
  :deploy (+ wt-deploy-mms-alerts);
}
note right
  us-persons-prod gate
  ("US citizen on US soil")
  Mandated by **FedRAMP High**
  (approval mechanism could be improved)
end note

if (any PROD-GOV deploy FAILURES?) then (yes)
  |Human|
  :approve-continue
  (gate required only after prod-gov failures);
  |Automated|
else (no — no gate)
endif

partition "INTERNAL" {
  :deploy;
}

:**RELEASED (backport)**
SHA live on prod / prod-gov / internal;
stop

@enduml
